---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/data/site.config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclosure"
  description="Our policies on affiliate links, sponsored content, and comped meals."
>
  <article class="py-12">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h1 class="text-bark-900 mb-8">Disclosure</h1>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p class="text-bark-500">Last updated: November 2024</p>

        <p>
          Transparency is important to us. This page explains how we make money and how
          that might affect our content. The short version: we're always honest, even
          when it's awkward.
        </p>

        <h2>Affiliate Links</h2>
        <p>
          Some links on this site are affiliate links. This means if you click and make
          a purchase, we may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          We only recommend products we actually use and believe in. Our affiliate
          relationships never influence our opinions—if we think something is overpriced
          or not worth it, we'll say so, even if we could earn a commission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Affiliate links help support this site and allow us to keep creating free content.
        </p>

        <h2>Sponsored Content</h2>
        <p>
          Sometimes brands pay us to create content featuring their products. When this
          happens, we always:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Clearly label the post as sponsored</li>
          <li>Only work with brands we genuinely like and use</li>
          <li>Maintain full editorial control—we write our honest opinions</li>
          <li>Disclose the relationship at the beginning of the content</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We turn down many more sponsorships than we accept. If we wouldn't use a
          product in our own kitchens, we won't promote it.
        </p>

        <h2>Restaurant Reviews</h2>
        <p>
          Most restaurant meals we review are ones we pay for ourselves. However, sometimes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Comped meals:</strong> A restaurant may provide a free meal for
            review purposes. We always disclose this at the top of the review.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sponsored reviews:</strong> Rarely, we accept payment to visit and
            review a restaurant. This is always clearly disclosed, and we maintain
            editorial independence—we never guarantee a positive review.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Every review includes a disclosure box indicating:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Whether we paid for the meal</li>
          <li>Whether any items were comped</li>
          <li>Whether the review is sponsored</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Our opinions are always our own. A comped meal doesn't buy a good review—just
          an honest one.
        </p>

        <h2>Free Products</h2>
        <p>
          We sometimes receive free products from brands hoping for coverage. Receiving
          a free product doesn't guarantee we'll feature it, and it certainly doesn't
          guarantee a positive review.
        </p>
        <p>
          When we do feature a product we received for free, we disclose that clearly.
        </p>

        <h2>Our Promise</h2>
        <p>
          We started {siteConfig.name} because we love food and cooking, not to get
          rich from affiliate links. While these revenue streams help keep the site
          running, they will never compromise our integrity.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you ever feel we've fallen short of these standards, please{' '}
          <a href="/contact">let us know</a>. We take your trust seriously.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions?</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about our disclosure policies, email us at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.social.email}`}>{siteConfig.social.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
